# Kept out of the build context, so a 50 GB working tree does not become a
# 50 GB upload to the docker daemon before the first instruction runs.
#
# Both images build from the repository ROOT:
#   docker build -f dockerfiles/gem5/Dockerfile -t manuel313/famaf_gem5:build .
#   docker build -f dockerfiles/CVA6/Dockerfile -t manuel313/famaf_cva6:build .

# History and tooling state. A submodule's .git is a file naming a gitdir
# outside the context, which would sit in the image as a dangling pointer. The
# CVA6 image makes its own repo for the one source whose commit is checked.
.git
**/.git
# These two describe the build context and this repository's submodules, so
# neither means anything inside an image.
.dockerignore
.gitmodules
.github
.gitlab-ci
.vscode
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Run artefacts. Every one of these is produced inside the container anyway,
# and the traces and VCDs alone run to tens of gigabytes.
**/*_trace.txt
**/*_trace.*.txt
**/*.vcd
**/*.vcd.*
**/*.fst
**/*.log
# Objdump listings from a run, but NOT the hand-written manifests upstream
# CVA6 keeps in ci/ and corev_apu/tb/, which the build reads.
gem5_config_CVA6/**/*.list
viewers/**/*.list
# What a run keeps is under results/. The rest are the simulators' own output
# and build trees, and tools/, which the CVA6 image builds for itself.
results/
verif/sim/out_*
m5out/
work-ver/
work-dpi/
build/
tools/

# The JSONs, which are large and regenerated from a trace or VCD: the tests/
# folders, a JSON beside a viewer's tracer, where its batch writes by default,
# and make_<Viewer>_oversized.py's output with its side files, wherever it is.
gem5_config_CVA6/gem5/tests/
gem5_config_CVA6/CVA6/tests/
viewers/*/tests/*.json
viewers/*/tests/*.js
viewers/*/*.json
**/oversized*.json*

# The project's mark and the fonts it is drawn from, which the documents in
# this repository use and nothing inside an image reads.
assets/

# Local scratch, the copies get_CVA6_files.py and get_gem5_files.py make, and
# what docker_sync.py pulls.
temp/
CVA6_files/
gem5_files/
container_results/

# The paper sources and their figures, which no image needs. The paper's
# Reference Core configuration is the exception: the gem5 image carries it
# under gem5_configs/CARLA2026/, so the published numbers can be reproduced.
viewers/*/docs/CARLA2026/
!viewers/*/docs/CARLA2026/gem5_config_Reference_Core.py
viewers/*/docs/old_versions/
viewers/*/docs/parser_phases/
